  "body": "Stacked on #1821 (merge #1821 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nFanuc, Doosan DNM and Mazak refuse a positive G83 dwell by name.\nZero-dwell G83 remains available.\nHaas keeps integer milliseconds and includes dwell in its G83 cycle signature.\nHaas writes P0 to clear a previous dwell.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe posts wrote P without checking G83 support for each control.\nHaas omitted dwell from its cycle signature and omitted zero P.\nThat could reuse an earlier dwell.\nFanuc's standard milling G83 format has no P.\nMazak's detailed format and summary disagree, so this post refuses dwell conservatively.\nThe decision record links the public control manuals and explains these limits.\n\n## Tests\n\nSeven pins pass in camcraft-post's g83_dwell suite:\n\n- fanuc_refuses_g83_dwell\n- mazak_refuses_g83_dwell\n- doosan_refuses_g83_dwell\n- g83_without_dwell_remains_available\n- haas_g83_writes_integer_milliseconds\n- haas_g83_updates_dwell_in_an_open_cycle_group\n- haas_g83_zero_dwell_clears_modal_p\n\nSix pins failed on unchanged posts.\nThe existing Haas milliseconds behavior passed before the fix.\nReplacing each of the four posts with upstream/main code made its affected pins fail.\nRestoring each fix made them pass.\nRemoving the Haas signature change and the P0 change separately also failed their pins.\nRestoring each change passed.\n\ncargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main passed with zero failures.\nThe final run took 18.2 minutes and included the expanded app integration selection.\ncargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings passed separately for camcraft-post and camcraft-app.\nThe initial gate hit a sandbox denial in the optional sccache preprocessor directory.\nCommand-line Cargo configuration disabled that cache and cleared RUSTC_WRAPPER for the successful gate.\nRepository configuration did not change.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\ncrates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_haas.nc adds P0 to its single G83 line.\nNo other golden change belongs to this issue.\nThe two-dot comparison against current upstream lists 139 golden files because the parent is older.\nEach was checked against base-1821.\nThe inherited differences comprise decimal formatting, G76 fixtures, and the six parent bore fixtures.\nOnly the synth_haas P0 word differs from the parent in this patch.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo real CNC control or GUI was exercised.\nDoosan OEM MV0009OPE241_v0 behavior was not publicly verified.\nMazak G83 dwell support remains ambiguous in the cited manual.\nOptional Fanuc small-hole mode is not selected by these posts.\nBatch and release gates were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #1821 changes onCycle in the same four posts.\nThis branch starts at its head, 1c06a3e1.\nPR #1738 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIts overlaps are formatting, block, toolNote, onParameter, afterOp and onProbeResult.\nNeither the new test nor the changed golden overlaps an open PR.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nChangelog: Refuse unsupported G83 dwell on Fanuc, Doosan and Mazak, and preserve or clear Haas G83 dwell correctly.\n\nFixes #1820\n",
